  "response_text": "The thread\u2019s stack was set up by creating a stack pointer to the stack and by setting the values of the thread\u2019s registers so that the computer thinks that the thread was already there. This way the thread will pop the register values into the hardware registers and will run the thread. If we do not store register values on the stack, the hardware will not pop the values onto the hardware registers, preventing the thread from executing. The way the registers are set up is the first entry on the stack is xPSR, the second is PC, then the link register and the general registers follow. If this order is not properly set, the thread may exhibit unexpected qualities or hard fault.\\n",
